# matc5b.cf -- t_matc.c coverage batch 5b: mlp/mlp1 (linear
# programming). Tableau layout and MAXIMIZE-with-<=-constraints
# convention read directly from lpf1()'s own doc comment (t_lp.c),
# not guessed: row 1 is the objective, rows 2.. are constraints with
# their RHS in the last column, and equality constraints (mlp1's own
# "p" count) must be the LAST rows of the constraint block. Checked
# against the textbook Reddy-Mikks-style LP (maximize 3x+5y subject
# to x<=4, 2y<=12, 3x+2y<=18): the known optimum (x=2, y=6, value=36)
# is reproduced exactly, and the dual solution satisfies
# complementary slackness and dual feasibility exactly by hand. mlp1
# repeats it with the third constraint (already tight at the optimum)
# turned into an equality, confirming the documented behaviour that
# equality constraints get their own dual value forced to 0.

silent = -1;

mdef(T,4,3) =   3, 5, 0,
                1, 0, 4,
                0, 2, 12,
                3, 2, 18;
mlp(T,X,Y);
mpr(X);
mpr(Y);

mlp1(T,1,X1,Y1);
mpr(X1);
mpr(Y1);
